result.skepticResultSchema:
Add to src/schemas.ts after reviewResultSchema/ReviewResult (after line 112), so it sits next to the schema it challenges:

```ts
export const skepticFindingVerdictSchema = z.object({
  ref: z.string().optional(),          // FR/AC ref when challenging a frAcFinding (e.g. "AC-INV-001.1")
  dimension: z.string().optional(),    // sleuth dimension when challenging a qualityGate dimension (e.g. "runtime_path")
  source: z.enum(["fr_ac_finding", "quality_dimension", "required_fix", "escalation"]),
  verdict: z.enum(["real", "refuted", "uncertain"]),
  severity: z.enum(["blocker", "major", "minor", "nit"]),
  reasoning: z.string(),
});

export const skepticResultSchema = z.object({
  status: z.enum(["upheld", "partially_refuted", "refuted", "uncertain"]),
  summary: z.string(),
  challengedReviewStatus: z.enum(["accepted", "repair_required", "blocked", "human_required"]),
  findingVerdicts: z.array(skepticFindingVerdictSchema),
  recommendation: z.string(),
});

export type SkepticFindingVerdict = z.infer<typeof skepticFindingVerdictSchema>;
export type SkepticResult = z.infer<typeof skepticResultSchema>;
```

Field rationale (chosen so RE-2 can later decide per-finding blocking without reopening this schema):
- status: skeptic's overall stance on the review's findings (independent of slice gate state).
- challengedReviewStatus: echoes the reviewResult.status being challenged so RE-2 can correlate the verdict to the exact review it judged without re-reading evidence ordering.
- findingVerdicts[]: one verdict per challenged item. `source` discriminates which part of the review it challenges (frAcFindings vs qualityGate.dimensions vs requiredFixes vs escalations); `ref`/`dimension` are the optional keys to join back to the review item. `verdict` (real|refuted|uncertain) + `severity` (blocker..nit) is exactly the (does-it-hold, how-much-does-it-matter) pair RE-2 needs to compute per-finding blocking. `reasoning` carries the independent justification.
- recommendation: free-text next-action, mirroring reviewResult.recommendation.

All objects are plain z.object (additionalProperties:false in output mode) so the SO-1 generator (writeSchemaFromZod) produces an equivalent-or-stricter JSON Schema with no hand-tuning, and schema-parity coverage applies cleanly. No nested .default() is used, so output/input required sets match (no qualityGate-style trap).

result.independenceGuard:
Required by RE-1's whole point: the skeptic must be a DISTINCT actor, never the worker or reviewer. Implement inside executeSkepticRun immediately after the driver-validation guard and BEFORE insertAgentRun (so a rejected request leaves no run/evidence/event residue).

```ts
const priorActors = input.store
  .listAgentRuns()
  .filter((r) => r.sliceId === slice.id && (r.role === "worker" || r.role === "reviewer"))
  .map((r) => r.actor);
if (priorActors.includes(input.actor)) {
  throw new Error(
    `Skeptic actor must be independent: '${input.actor}' already acted as worker/reviewer on slice ${slice.id}. Use a distinct --actor.`,
  );
}
```

Notes:
- Keys off AgentRunRecord.role (worker runs set role:"worker" at cli.ts:2425; reviewer runs role:"reviewer" at cli.ts:2679), so it precisely targets the two roles whose independence RE-1 protects. recovery/verifier/overseer actors are intentionally NOT blocked.
- It throws (not a soft event) so the CLI exits non-zero — directly satisfies test (c). The throw propagates out of executeSkepticRun to the command's try/finally, which still closes the store.
- It does not consult chat/memory — independence is derived from the durable agent-run ledger, honoring the rollup-from-ledger non-negotiable.

result.cliCommand:
Add a `swarm skeptic` command mirroring `swarm review` (cli.ts:921-945), placed right after the review command block:

```ts
program
  .command("skeptic")
  .description("Run an independent skeptic that challenges the latest review findings for a slice")
  .argument("<slice-id>", "slice identifier")
  .option("--actor <actor>", "skeptic actor id shown in observability (must be distinct from worker/reviewer)", "skeptic")
  .option("--driver <driver>", "skeptic driver (fixture or a registered driver)", "codex")
  .option("--model <model>", "model override passed to the skeptic driver")
  .action(async (sliceId: string, options: { actor: string; driver: string; model?: string }) => {
    const workspace = resolveWorkspace();
    ensureInitialized(workspace);
    const store = new SwarmStore(workspace);
    try {
      const result = await executeSkepticRun({
        workspace,
        store,
        sliceId,
        actor: options.actor,
        driver: parseWorkerDriver(options.driver),
        model: options.model,
      });
      printSkepticRunResult(result);
    } finally {
      store.close();
    }
  });
```

